<title>USA: Tremont Q1 operating profit before charge.</title>
<headline>Tremont Q1 operating profit before charge.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>TREMONT CORP</p>
<p>						 Quarter ended March 31,</p>
<p>						1997		     1996</p>
<p>Equity in earnings (losses) of:</p>
<p>   TIMET				     $4.8		    $1.3</p>
<p>   NL Industries			  (7.2)		     1.4</p>
<p>   Other					3.9		     ---</p>
<p>						  1.5		     2.7</p>
<p>Corporate expenses, net</p>
<p>   of interest income		     ---			.3</p>
<p> Interest expense			   ---			.1</p>
<p>Income before taxes</p>
<p>   and minority interest		  1.5		     2.3</p>
<p> Income tax expense			 2.9		     ---</p>
<p> Minority interest			  1.0			.1</p>
<p>   Net income			     (2.4)		     2.2</p>
<p> Net income per common share	  (.32)		     .29</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs				7.6		     7.4</p>
<p>		     (In millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q1 1997 loss included company's 18% equity in NL Industries, whose results included a $30 million charge related to the adoption of a new accounting standard for environmental remediation liabilities and represented a loss to Tremont of $.70 per share.</p>
</text>
